feat(hmi_manager): add screen manager with PNG splash screen support

Implement a two-phase screen manager architecture that allows static
PNG assets stored in flash to be displayed via LVGL 9.x on the
ST7796 480x320 display.

## Screen Manager Architecture

Two-phase initialization to respect LVGL thread-safety constraints:

Phase 1 - screen_manager_init() called from main() before threads:
  Creates bare lv_obj_t skeletons for all screens (no assets).
  Safe to call before lvgl_thread starts because lv_obj_create(NULL)
  does not trigger rendering.

Phase 2 - screen_manager_setup_assets() called from lvgl_thread:
  Attaches lv_img assets and builds widget tree inside LVGL context.
  This is mandatory - lv_img_create() must run in lvgl_thread only.

Screens:
  SCREEN_SPLASH    (0) - BifrostOX2 PNG splash screen
  SCREEN_DASHBOARD (1) - existing LVGL widgets dashboard
  SCREEN_BLACK     (2) - blank black screen

Button mapping:
  BTN6 -> SCREEN_DASHBOARD
  BTN7 -> SCREEN_SPLASH
  BTN8 -> SCREEN_BLACK

## Asset Pipeline (scripts/codetools/)

preview.py:
  Converts any image to 480x320 RGB565-simulated PNG for visual
  validation before embedding. Output suffix: _lcd.png.
  Fit modes: stretch (default), contain, crop.
  Run without args to batch-process all images in assets/png/.

png2code.py:
  Converts *_lcd.png files to LVGL 9.x compatible C arrays.
  Format: LV_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB565, little-endian uint16_t, stored
  in .rodata (flash). Zero RAM copy - LVGL reads via pointer.
  Reverse mode (--reverse): reconstructs _reverse.png from C array
  for display emulation without hardware.
  Run without args to batch-process all *_lcd.png in assets/png/.

Workflow:
  1. Designer exports PNG at any resolution
  2. ./preview.py          -> generates *_lcd.png (480x320, RGB565 sim)
  3. ./png2code.py         -> generates uiux/assets/<symbol>.c
  4. make && flash         -> asset visible on display
  5. ./png2code.py --reverse -> verify output matches display

## Flash note

OpenOCD must be invoked with DUAL_BANK=1 when firmware exceeds
Bank 0 (1024KB). Standard FLASH_STM32H7x alias does not configure
Bank 1, causing HardFault on boot when .rodata crosses 0x08100000.

Correct flash command:
  openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg \
          -c "set DUAL_BANK 1" \
          -f target/stm32h7x.cfg \
          -c "init" \
          -c "reset halt" \
          -c "flash write_image erase nuttx.bin 0x08000000" \
          -c "reset run"

